{
    "background_story": "Eloise was a free-spirited artist living in the Montmartre quarter of Paris in the early 20th century. She was deeply inspired by the works of Guillaume Apollinaire, the French poet and art critic who was a key figure in the Cubist movement. Eloise's own art reflected the same sense of experimentation and innovation, as she pushed the boundaries of traditional techniques and mediums. Her studio was a hub of creative energy, where artists and writers would gather to discuss the latest ideas and trends. Eloise's relationship with Apollinaire was one of mutual admiration and respect, and she was known to have modeled for several of his artist friends, including Pablo Picasso. Her life was a testament to the bohemian spirit of the time, and her art continues to be celebrated for its boldness and originality.",
